This solves a problem `setControlCallback` can't: when the DAW automation moves the filter frequency, the label updates automatically because `attachToModuleParameter` catches changes from any source.

### Preset-Aware UI Updates

When a preset loads, components with `saveInPreset` are restored automatically — but side effects (switching sample maps, rebuilding panel content, resetting visual state) need manual handling. A Broadcaster chain keeps this organized:

```javascript
const var presetBC = Engine.createBroadcaster({
    id: "presetLoaded",
    args: ["presetName"]
});

// Fire after preset load completes
presetBC.addListener(0, "refreshSamplers",
    function(presetName)
    {
        // Reload sample maps based on new preset state
        sampler.loadSampleMap(getCurrentMap());
    });

presetBC.addDelayedListener(100, 0, "refreshUI",
    function(presetName)
    {
        // Rebuild dynamic UI elements after a short delay
        rebuildPanels();
    });
```

The delayed listener ensures the UI refresh happens after all component values have settled. Multiple independent targets keep the concerns separated — sampler logic doesn't know about UI rebuilds.

For advanced Broadcaster patterns — EQ parameter coordination, drag-bypass interaction, centralized state bus architecture, and cross-Broadcaster event chains — see [Broadcaster Patterns](/v2/examples/broadcaster-patterns).

