name: setRange
params:
  - { name: min, type: int, desc: "Start position in samples (inclusive)" }
  - { name: max, type: int, desc: "End position in samples (exclusive)" }
---
::

```javascript
af.setRange(0, 44100);
```


Sets the active sample range within the loaded audio file. After calling this, `getContent()` and `getNumSamples()` operate on the selected sub-range only. The range is clamped to valid bounds automatically. This has the same effect as dragging the sample range interactively in a ScriptAudioWaveform component.

#### Example

```javascript
// Paste in the code to load the asset from above...

// clear the audio file (so that it loads the full file again
// when you recompile)
audioFile.loadFile("");

// load the first asset (again)
audioFile.loadFile(firstAsset);

// Define the new sample range
var minSample = 1000;
var maxSample = 5000;

// Grab the full sample data
var fullSample = audioFile.getContent();

Console.print(fullSample[0].length); // 830117

// Set the new sample range using the setRange method
audioFile.setRange(minSample, maxSample);

// Now the getContent() method will only return the slice
// from 1000 to 5000
var slice = audioFile.getContent();

Console.print(slice[0].length); // 4000
```

