name: addModuleParameterSyncer
params:
  - { name: moduleId, type: String, desc: "The ID of the target processor module" }
  - { name: parameterIndex, type: var, desc: "Parameter identifier -- either a string parameter name or an integer index" }
  - { name: metadata, type: var, desc: "Listener metadata -- a string ID or JSON object with at least an `id` field" }
---
::

```javascript
bc.addModuleParameterSyncer("SimpleGain1", "Gain", "gainSync");
```


Adds a target that synchronises a module parameter from the broadcaster's last argument value. When the broadcaster fires, the final argument is applied to the specified parameter on the target module. The `parameterIndex` can be a string parameter name or an integer index.

::warning{title="Enables synchronous execution for broadcaster"}
This method forces the entire broadcaster into synchronous execution mode. All subsequent sends - including `sendAsyncMessage` - execute synchronously. This is a broadcaster-level side effect, not scoped to this syncer.
::

