::method-heading{name="reset"}
::

```javascript
bc.reset();
```

Dispatches the broadcaster's original default values (from construction) to all listeners, bypassing change detection and the bypass check. This does not clear the stored values, remove listeners, or remove sources - it only re-dispatches the defaults.

::warning{title="Undefined defaults suppress reset dispatch"}
For broadcasters created with the standard `{ id: "...", args: [...] }` format, all default values are `undefined`, so `reset()` has no visible effect - the undefined-argument check suppresses the dispatch.
