Throws a script error with the provided error message if `condition` is false. This is the most flexible assertion method, allowing you to specify exactly what went wrong.

#### Basic

```javascript
// Context: When assertTrue would be cryptic, assertWithMessage provides
// context-specific error messages that include runtime values.

const var index = -5;

Console.assertWithMessage(index >= 0, "Index must not be negative, got: " + index);
```

