::method-heading
---
name: sample
params:
  - { name: label, type: String, desc: "A descriptive label for this data sample point." }
  - { name: dataToSample, type: var, desc: "The data to record. The value is cloned at capture time. Any type is accepted." }
---
::

Records a labeled snapshot of data into the active sampling session. The data is cloned at capture time, so subsequent mutations do not affect the recorded value. Requires `startSampling()` to be called first.

::warning{title="Requires active sampling session"}
Without an active session, `sample()` logs a warning and skips recording. The warning is only shown once per Console instance - subsequent calls without a session are silently skipped.
::

#### Example

```javascript
{
	.sample("my session"); // starts a sampling session until the block is done

	var x = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];

	// creates a snapshot of the array and stores it as the first label
	Console.sample("first", x);

	x[2] = 0;

	// creates a snapshot of the array and stores it under the second label
	Console.sample("second", x);
}
```

