name: getSemitonesFromPitchRatio
params:
  - { name: pitchRatio, type: double, desc: "Pitch ratio to convert. 1.0 = unity, 2.0 = one octave up, 0.5 = one octave down." }
---
::

```javascript
var semitones = Engine.getSemitonesFromPitchRatio(2.0);
```


Converts a pitch ratio to cents (not semitones, despite the method name) using the formula `1200 * log2(ratio)`. A ratio of 2.0 returns 1200.0 (one octave), not 12.0. Divide the result by 100 to get semitones.

::warning{title="Returns cents, not semitones"}
This method returns cents, not semitones. It is not a true inverse of `Engine.getPitchRatioFromSemitones()`, which expects semitones as input.
::

::see-also
