::method-heading{name="getRedirectedFolder"}
::

```javascript
var resolved = f.getRedirectedFolder();
```

Checks this directory for a HISE link file and returns the redirect target if one exists. HISE uses platform-specific link files (`LinkWindows`, `LinkOSX`, `LinkLinux`) inside directories to redirect folder references to a different location - the same mechanism used for sample folder redirection. If no link file is found, returns this same File object.

::warning{title="Link files are platform-specific"}
The link file name is platform-specific. A redirect configured on one platform (e.g. `LinkWindows`) is not followed on another. Calling this on a path that exists as a regular file triggers a script error, but calling it on a non-existent path silently returns the same File object.
::

#### Resolve Link Redirect

```javascript
// Context: Accessing the actual preset or sample directory, which may be
//          redirected to an external drive via a LinkWindows/LinkOSX file

const var presetDir = FileSystem.getFolder(FileSystem.UserPresets);

// Follow any link file redirect to the actual location
const var resolvedDir = presetDir.getChildFile("Presets").getRedirectedFolder();

Console.print("Actual preset location: " + resolvedDir.toString(0));

// Now use the resolved directory for file operations
var presetFiles = FileSystem.findFiles(resolvedDir, "*.preset", true);
Console.print("Found " + presetFiles.length + " presets");
```

