name: applyMask
params:
  - { name: path, type: Object, desc: "A Path object defining the mask shape" }
  - { name: area, type: Array, desc: "Bounding rectangle `[x, y, w, h]` to scale the path into" }
  - { name: invert, type: int, desc: "If true, areas outside the path are kept instead of inside" }
---
::

```javascript
g.applyMask(myPath, [0, 0, 200, 200], false);
```


Applies a path-based alpha mask to the current layer. Pixels inside the path are kept and pixels outside are made transparent. Set `invert` to `true` to reverse this behaviour (keep pixels outside the path instead).

::warning{title="Non-uniform scaling distorts mask shape"}
The path is scaled to fit the area with non-uniform scaling. If the path's aspect ratio does not match the area's, the mask shape will be distorted.
::

#### Applymask Circular

```javascript
Panel1.setPaintRoutine(function(g)
{
    var area = [0, 0, this.getWidth(), this.getHeight()];

    g.beginLayer(false);
    g.fillAll(0xFFFF0000);
    g.setColour(0xFF0000FF);
    g.fillRect([20, 20, 60, 60]);

    var p = Content.createPath();
    p.addEllipse(area);
    g.applyMask(p, area, false);
    g.endLayer();
});
```

