name: drawRepaintMarker
params:
  - { name: label, type: String, desc: "Identifier for Perfetto profiling traces" }
---
::

```javascript
g.drawRepaintMarker("MyPanel");
```


Fills the entire component area with a random semi-transparent colour to visually indicate that a repaint has occurred. Each call produces a different random colour, making it easy to see how often a component repaints - rapid colour changes indicate excessive repainting. Place this at the start or end of a paint routine during development to diagnose performance issues. The `label` parameter is used for Perfetto profiling traces when available.

#### Drawrepaintmarker Debug

```javascript
// Context: Add drawRepaintMarker at the end of a paint routine during
// development to see how often the panel repaints. Rapid colour changes
// indicate the panel is repainting too frequently. Use a conditional
// flag so the marker can be toggled without removing code.

const var DEBUG_REPAINT = true;

const var bgPanel = Content.addPanel("bgPanel", 0, 0);
bgPanel.set("width", 200);
bgPanel.set("height", 100);

bgPanel.setPaintRoutine(function(g)
{
    g.fillAll(0xFF333333);
    g.setColour(0xFFCCCCCC);
    g.setFont("regular", 14.0);
    g.drawAlignedText("Content", [10, 10, 180, 30], "left");

    // Shows a random colour overlay on each repaint
    if (DEBUG_REPAINT)
        g.drawRepaintMarker(this.get("id"));
});
```

