name: setUpdateCallback
params:
  - { name: callback, type: Function, desc: "Callback invoked on macro connection changes" }
---
::

```javascript
mh.setUpdateCallback(onMacroUpdate);
```


Registers a callback that fires whenever macro connections change. The callback receives the full connection array (same format as `MacroHandler.getMacroDataObject()` output) as its argument. Only one callback can be active at a time - calling this again replaces the previous one. You can pass a Broadcaster instead of a plain function to fan out change notifications to multiple independent listeners.

::warning{title="Fires immediately on registration"}
The callback fires immediately on registration with the current macro state. If you call this during `onInit`, the callback body runs synchronously before the next line of init code executes.
::

#### Broadcaster Macro Callback (validated)

```javascript
// Context: Instead of a plain function, pass a Broadcaster to fan out
// macro change notifications to multiple independent listeners

const var mh = Engine.createMacroHandler();

// Create a broadcaster that will receive macro change events
const var macroBroadcaster = Engine.createBroadcaster({
    "id": "macroBroadcaster",
    "args": ["macroData"]
});

// The broadcaster itself becomes the callback - when macro connections
// change, it fires as a broadcaster message that any number of listeners
// can subscribe to
mh.setUpdateCallback(macroBroadcaster);

var listenerCount = 0;

// Now multiple independent listeners can react to macro changes
macroBroadcaster.addListener("", "update macro indicators", function(macroData)
{
    // Update UI indicators showing which macros are connected
    listenerCount++;
    Console.print("Active connections: " + macroData.length);
});

macroBroadcaster.addListener("", "sync context menu state", function(macroData)
{
    // Update context menu enabled/checked states
    for (item in macroData)
        Console.print("Slot " + item.MacroIndex + ": " + item.Attribute);
});
```

