```javascript
Message.setVelocity(100);
```


Sets the velocity of the current note-on event. Only works in `onNoteOn` - not `onNoteOff` or other callbacks. For a level property that works across all event types and both note-on and note-off, use `Message.setGain()` instead.

::warning{title="Zero velocity may trigger note-off"}
Always ensure the velocity is at least 1. A velocity of 0 is technically valid in HISE, but downstream MIDI output or DAW processing may interpret it as a note-off per the MIDI specification.
::

#### Velocity Curve Reshaping

```javascript
// Context: A velocity table modifies the incoming velocity to match
// the instrument's dynamic response. The table provides a normalized
// curve (0.0-1.0 input/output) that reshapes the velocity distribution.

const var veloTable = Content.addTable("VeloTable", 10, 10);
veloTable.set("height", 200);
veloTable.set("width", 400);

const var table = veloTable.registerAtParent(0);

function onNoteOn()
{
    // Map velocity through the table curve
    local v = 127.0 * table.getTableValueNormalised(Message.getVelocity() / 127.0);

    Message.setVelocity(parseInt(Math.max(1, v)));
}
```

