name: connectToPanel
params:
  - { name: panel, type: Object, desc: "A ScriptPanel component reference." }
---
::

```javascript
mp.connectToPanel(Panel1);
```


Connects this player to a ScriptPanel for automatic UI updates. The panel receives `repaint()` calls when new MIDI content is loaded, when the track or sequence selection changes, when the sequence is cleared, and when events are flushed. To also repaint during playback (e.g. to draw a moving cursor), call `setRepaintOnPositionChange(true)`. Use `getNoteRectangleList()` and `getPlaybackPosition()` inside the paint routine to render the current state.

#### Piano Roll Visualization

```javascript
// Context: Connect a MidiPlayer to a ScriptPanel for automatic repainting
// when the sequence changes, and draw notes using getNoteRectangleList()

const var mp = Synth.getMidiPlayer("MidiPlayer1");
const var PianoRoll = Content.addPanel("PianoRoll", 0, 0);

// Connect so the panel repaints when the sequence changes
mp.connectToPanel(PianoRoll);

PianoRoll.setPaintRoutine(function(g)
{
    g.fillAll(0xFF666666);

    var rList = mp.getNoteRectangleList([0, 0, this.getWidth(), this.getHeight()]);

    g.setColour(Colours.white);

    for (r in rList)
        g.fillRect(r);
});
```

