::method-heading{name="getEventList"}
::

```javascript
var events = mp.getEventList();
```

Returns an array of MessageHolder objects for all MIDI events in the current sequence's current track. Each MessageHolder wraps a note number, velocity, channel, and timestamp. Timestamps are in samples by default or in ticks if `setUseTimestampInTicks(true)` was called. Note-on and note-off events are paired with consecutive event IDs, so you can find the matching note-off for a note-on by comparing `getEventId()`. Call `flushMessageList()` after processing to apply changes.

::warning{title="Never reorder note-on/note-off pairs"}
Never reorder note-on/note-off pairs in the event list - if a note-off appears before its matching note-on, playback behaviour will be unpredictable. Use `Engine.getQuarterBeatsForSamples()` and related helpers to convert between timestamp domains.
::

#### Filter Events By Note Number

```javascript
// Context: Extract events, filter by type and note number, and compute
// step positions from tick timestamps for a step sequencer UI

const var mp = Synth.getMidiPlayer("MidiPlayer1");
var events = mp.getEventList();
var tpq = mp.getTicksPerQuarter(); // 960

// Filter to only note-on events for a specific note
var noteOns = events.filter(function(e)
{
    return e.isNoteOn() && e.getNoteNumber() == 64;
});

// Convert tick timestamps to step positions (16th note grid)
var stepSize = tpq / 4; // 240 ticks per 16th note

for (e in noteOns)
{
    var stepIndex = parseInt(e.getTimestamp() / stepSize);
    var velocity = e.getVelocity() / 127.0;
    Console.print("Step " + stepIndex + ": velocity " + velocity);
}
```

#### Read Modify Write Transpose

```javascript
// Context: Get the event list, modify events in place, then flush back.
// This is the standard edit workflow for MIDI data.

const var mp = Synth.getMidiPlayer("MidiPlayer1");
var events = mp.getEventList();

for (e in events)
{
    if (e.isNoteOn() || e.isNoteOff())
        e.setNoteNumber(e.getNoteNumber() + 12);
}

mp.flushMessageList(events);
```

