name: setUseGlobalUndoManager
params:
  - { name: shouldUseGlobalUndoManager, type: int, desc: "Whether to enable the global undo manager." }
---
::

```javascript
mp.setUseGlobalUndoManager(true);
```


Switches from the default per-player undo manager to the global undo stack shared with `Engine.undo()`. By default each MidiPlayer has its own dedicated undo manager, so `undo()` and `redo()` work without calling this method. Enabling the global manager lets MIDI edits participate in the same undo history as UI parameter changes.

::warning{title="Shared stack, disabling destroys history"}
The global undo stack is shared across all MidiPlayer instances and UI actions, so MIDI edits may interleave with parameter changes. Calling this method with `false` after enabling it destroys the per-player undo manager - you must call it with `true` again to re-attach to the global stack, and the previous per-player history is lost.
::

#### Enable Undo For Sequencer

```javascript
// Context: Enable the global undo manager during initialization so that
// all subsequent MIDI edits (flushMessageList, setTimeSignature) can be
// undone with Engine.undo()

const var mp = Synth.getMidiPlayer("MidiPlayer1");
mp.setUseGlobalUndoManager(true);
mp.setUseTimestampInTicks(true);
mp.create(4, 4, 1);

// Create and flush some test data
var noteList = [];
var on = Engine.createMessageHolder();
var off = Engine.createMessageHolder();
on.setType(on.NoteOn);
off.setType(on.NoteOff);
on.setNoteNumber(60);
off.setNoteNumber(60);
on.setVelocity(100);
on.setChannel(1);
off.setChannel(1);
on.setTimestamp(0);
off.setTimestamp(960);
noteList.push(on);
noteList.push(off);
mp.flushMessageList(noteList);

// Undo reverts the edit
Engine.undo();
```

