name: getIntersection
params:
  - { name: start, type: Array, desc: "Start point of the test line as `[x, y]`." }
  - { name: end, type: Array, desc: "End point of the test line as `[x, y]`." }
  - { name: keepSectionOutsidePath, type: int, desc: "If `true`, returns the outer endpoint of the clipped line; if `false`, returns the inner endpoint where the line enters the path." }
---
::

```javascript
var pt = p.getIntersection([0, 50], [200, 50], false);
```


Tests whether a line segment from `start` to `end` intersects the path. If an intersection exists, returns the intersection point as `[x, y]`. The `keepSectionOutsidePath` flag controls which endpoint of the clipped line is returned: `true` for the outer point, `false` for the entry point into the path.

::warning{title="Returns false when no intersection found"}
Returns `false` (not an array) when no intersection is found. Always check the return type before indexing the result.
::

#### Path Intersection Test

```javascript
const var p = Content.createPath();
p.addEllipse([0, 0, 100, 100]);

var intersection = p.getIntersection([0, 50], [100, 50], false);

if (intersection)
    Console.print("Hit at: " + intersection[0] + ", " + intersection[1]);
else
    Console.print("No intersection");
```

