::method-heading
---
name: setFileDropCallback
params:
  - { name: callbackLevel, type: String, desc: "The file drop callback level" }
  - { name: wildcard, type: String, desc: "File extension filter" }
  - { name: dropFunction, type: Function, desc: "Callback function receiving file drop information" }
---
::

```javascript
pnl.setFileDropCallback("Drop Only", "*.wav", onFileDrop);
```


Registers a callback for file drag-and-drop events. The callback level controls which events fire:

| Level | Events |
|-------|--------|
| `"No Callbacks"` | Disabled (default) |
| `"Drop Only"` | Fires only when files are dropped |
| `"Drop & Hover"` | Also fires when files enter or exit the panel |
| `"All Callbacks"` | Also fires on mouse movement during drag |

The wildcard filters accepted file types (e.g. `"*.wav;*.aif"`). Use `"{FOLDER}"` as the wildcard to accept only folder drops. Pass an empty string to deactivate the callback.

The callback receives a JSON object with `x`, `y`, `hover`, `drop`, and `fileName` properties. The `fileName` is only present on drop events and contains the absolute path (or an array of paths for multi-file drops). Use `FileSystem.fromAbsolutePath()` to convert a dropped path to a File object.

To persist a dropped filename in a user preset, wrap it in a JSON object before calling `setValue()` - raw String values are not permitted as preset values.

::warning{title="Non-matching files silently ignored"}
The wildcard filter is checked before the callback fires. Files that do not match are silently ignored with no callback.
::

#### Example

```javascript
Panel1.setFileDropCallback("All Callbacks", "*.wav", function(f)
{
    if(f.drop)
    {
        // We can't pass in only the filename
        // (a String is forbidden as preset value in order
        // to prevent subtle bugs) so we need to create
        // a simple object with a single property
        var x = {};
        x.fileName = f.fileName;

        // We could also just have passed in f to the function,
        // but this reduces the noise a bit
        this.setValue(x);
        this.changed();
    }
});

inline function onPanel1Control(component, value)
{
    // This might be empty (at initialisation or for whatever reason)...
    if(isDefined(value.fileName))
    {
        var myFile = FileSystem.fromAbsolutePath(value.fileName);
        // Do something with myFile...
    }
};
```

