::method-heading
---
name: setUsePreallocatedLength
params:
  - { name: length, type: int, desc: "Maximum number of sliders to preallocate for, or 0 to disable" }
---
::

```javascript
spd.setUsePreallocatedLength(32);
```


Configures a fixed-size preallocated buffer for the slider data. Once set, `setNumSliders()` calls up to the preallocated limit adjust a view into this fixed block without allocating new memory, preserving all existing values - including those beyond the current view that become visible again when the count increases. Pass 0 to disable preallocation and return to normal allocation behaviour. Call this immediately after creation for any slider pack whose count changes at runtime (e.g. variable-length step sequencers).

#### Batch Preallocated Sequencer (validated)

```javascript
// Context: A step sequencer with multiple channels and parameter modes
// needs many SliderPackData objects that resize without reallocation.

const var NUM_CHANNELS = 4;
const var NUM_MODES = 3;  // e.g., velocity, pitch, probability
const var MAX_STEPS = 32;

const var packs = [];
reg packIndex = 0;

for (i = 0; i < NUM_CHANNELS * NUM_MODES; i++)
{
    packs.push(Engine.createAndRegisterSliderPackData(packIndex));
    packs[packIndex].setNumSliders(MAX_STEPS);
    packs[packIndex].setAllValues(0.0);
    packs[packIndex++].setUsePreallocatedLength(MAX_STEPS);
}

// Later: resize without allocation or value loss
packs[0].setValue(0, 0.8);
packs[0].setNumSliders(16);  // View narrows, value at index 0 preserved
packs[0].setNumSliders(32);  // View widens, all original values still intact

Console.print(packs[0].getValue(0)); // 0.8
```

