::method-heading
---
name: addEffect
params:
  - { name: type, type: String, desc: "Effect processor type name (e.g., \"SimpleGain\", \"SimpleReverb\")" }
  - { name: id, type: String, desc: "Unique ID for the new effect" }
  - { name: index, type: int, desc: "Insertion position in the effect chain" }
---
::

```javascript
var fx = Synth.addEffect("SimpleGain", "NewGain", -1);
```


Dynamically adds an effect to the parent synth's effect chain at runtime and returns a `ScriptEffect` handle. If an effect with the same `id` already exists in the chain, the existing processor is returned instead of creating a duplicate. The `index` parameter controls insertion position: `-1` appends to the end, while a non-negative value inserts before the effect at that index. Audio processing is briefly suspended during the operation.

#### Add Effect Basic

```javascript
const var gain = Synth.addEffect("SimpleGain", "ScriptGain", -1);
gain.setBypassed(true);
```

