name: addTablePoint
params:
  - { name: x, type: double, desc: "Normalized horizontal position of the new point" }
  - { name: y, type: double, desc: "Normalized vertical value at this point" }
---
::

```javascript
td.addTablePoint(0.5, 0.8);
```


Adds a new control point at the given normalised coordinates with a default curve factor of 0.5 (linear). For building curves with multiple points, prefer `setTablePointsFromArray()` which sets all points in one call.

::warning{title="Each call re-renders full lookup table"}
Each call triggers a full lookup table re-render. Calling `addTablePoint()` in a loop is significantly slower than a single `setTablePointsFromArray()` call with the complete point array.
::

