Makes this Table handle refer to the same underlying data as another Table object. After linking, both handles share the same control points and lookup table - modifications through either handle affect both. Callbacks registered on this handle remain active and fire based on the linked data's events.

#### Link Two Tables (validated)

```javascript
const var td1 = Engine.createAndRegisterTableData(0);
const var td2 = Engine.createAndRegisterTableData(1);

// Set a custom curve on td1
td1.setTablePointsFromArray([
    [0.0, 0.0, 0.5],
    [0.5, 1.0, 0.5],
    [1.0, 0.0, 0.5]
]);

// Link td2 to td1 -- they now share the same data
td2.linkTo(td1);

// Querying td2 returns td1's curve
var val = td2.getTableValueNormalised(0.5);
```

