::method-heading
---
name: setFinishCallback
params:
  - { name: newFinishCallback, type: Function, desc: "The finish callback function" }
---
::

```javascript
bt.setFinishCallback(onTaskFinished);
```


Sets the callback that fires when a background task starts and finishes. The callback receives two boolean arguments: `isFinished` and `wasCancelled`. It is called with `(false, false)` at task start, `(true, false)` on normal completion, and `(true, true)` on abort. The BackgroundTask is available as `this` inside the callback.

::warning{title="Callback may run concurrently with task"}
The finish callback runs on the scripting thread and may execute concurrently with the still-running background task function. Avoid accessing shared state without the thread-safe property store.
::

::warning{title="Only triggered by callOnBackgroundThread"}
Not triggered by `killVoicesAndCall()` - only by `callOnBackgroundThread()` and `runProcess()`.
::

#### Finish Callback Protocol

```javascript
const var bt = Engine.createBackgroundTask("StatusTask");

inline function onTaskFinished(isFinished, wasCancelled)
{
    if (!isFinished)
        Console.print("Task started");
    else if (wasCancelled)
        Console.print("Task was cancelled");
    else
        Console.print("Task completed successfully");
};

bt.setFinishCallback(onTaskFinished);
```

