name: setTimeOut
params:
  - { name: newTimeout, type: int, desc: "Timeout in milliseconds" }
---
::

```javascript
bt.setTimeOut(1000);
```


Sets the timeout in milliseconds for thread stop operations (default: 500). This value controls how long `sendAbortSignal(true)` blocks, how long starting a new task waits for the old thread to stop, and how much time each `shouldAbort()` call adds to the script engine timeout. Estimate the right value from the longest interval between `shouldAbort()` calls in your task function, then add headroom for slower machines.

#### Example

```javascript
function myTask(thread)
{
	for(i = 0; i < 1000000; i++)
	{
		if(thread.shouldAbort())
			break;

		subFunctionThatTakes900MillisecondsPerRun();
	}
}
```

