::method-heading{name="shouldAbort"}
::

```javascript
var abort = bt.shouldAbort();
```

Checks whether the thread has been signalled to stop and extends the script engine timeout. Returns true if `sendAbortSignal()` was called or the script is being recompiled. Each call extends the timeout by the configured value, preventing the watchdog from killing long-running tasks. Call this at least once per loop iteration - failing to do so means the task cannot be cancelled and the script engine timeout is not extended.

