Updates the parameter's range from a JSON object. You only need to specify the properties you want to change - missing properties receive defaults:

| Property | Default |
|----------|---------|
| `MinValue` | 0.0 |
| `MaxValue` | 1.0 |
| `SkewFactor` | 1.0 |
| `StepSize` | 0.0 (continuous) |
| `Inverted` | false |

This method supports undo via the parent node's UndoManager, unlike `setRangeProperty()` which does not.

#### Range From Object

```javascript
const var nw = Synth.getExistingDspNetwork("myNetwork");
const var nd = nw.get("myOsc");
const var p = nd.getOrCreateParameter("Frequency");

// Only specify what differs from defaults
p.setRangeFromObject({
    "MinValue": 20.0,
    "MaxValue": 20000.0,
    "SkewFactor": 0.3
});

// Read back -- StepSize and Inverted have defaults
var range = p.getRangeObject();
Console.print(range.MinValue);   // 20
Console.print(range.StepSize);   // 0
Console.print(range.Inverted);   // 0
```

