::method-heading{name="getOpenGLStatistics"}
::

```javascript
var stats = shd.getOpenGLStatistics();
```

Returns a JSON object with information about the GPU and OpenGL context. The returned object contains these properties:

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `VersionString` | String | Full GL version string |
| `Major` | int | GL major version number |
| `Minor` | int | GL minor version number |
| `Vendor` | String | GPU vendor name |
| `Renderer` | String | GPU model name |
| `GLSL Version` | String | Supported shader language version |

If no OpenGL context is active, the properties contain placeholder values ("Inactive" and zero).

::warning{title="Only available after first render"}
The statistics object is populated during the first GPU compilation pass on the render thread. Calling this before the shader has been rendered at least once returns `undefined`.
::

#### Gl Statistics Query

```javascript
const var pnl = Content.addPanel("ShaderPanel", 0, 0);
const var shd = Content.createShader("");

pnl.setPaintRoutine(function(g)
{
    g.applyShader(shd, [0, 0, this.getWidth(), this.getHeight()]);
});

// After the first render, query GPU info
var stats = shd.getOpenGLStatistics();

if (isDefined(stats))
{
    Console.print("GPU: " + stats.Renderer);
    Console.print("OpenGL: " + stats.Major + "." + stats.Minor);
}
```

